      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(google): add typed Gemini CLI auth boundary",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe bundled Google/Gemini CLI auth boundary needs to support two real cases without leaking raw auth-profile objects across the CLI backend boundary:\n\n- `google` API-backed profiles use API-key credentials.\n- `google-gemini-cli` direct Gemini CLI profiles use OAuth credentials staged into an isolated Gemini CLI auth home.\n\nThe previous branch made the boundary Google-specific and also removed Gemini CLI API-key staging behavior that existing Google API-key profiles relied on. That meant generic CLI backends could document `authProfileForwarding` but never receive resolved credentials, and Gemini CLI API-key usage regressed.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added a public provider hook, `resolveCliBackendAuthCredential`, for provider-owned CLI backend credential resolution.\n- Added generic fallback forwarding for standard auth-profile credentials as typed envelopes: `api_key`, `token`, and `oauth`.\n- Updated CLI run preparation to resolve forwarded credentials through the selected provider hook first, then the generic fallback.\n- Preserved backend allowlist checks before and after credential resolution.\n- Restored Gemini CLI API-key staging via `GEMINI_API_KEY` while keeping OAuth file staging isolated.\n- Allowed the Gemini CLI backend to accept `google` API-key profiles and `google-gemini-cli` OAuth profiles explicitly.\n- Fixed cleanup gaps when preparation fails after MCP/skills resources are prepared.\n- Made bundled MCP fail closed when loopback startup fails instead of writing a partial config.\n- Updated Plugin SDK exports and regenerated the Plugin SDK API baseline.\n- Updated CLI backend plugin docs for provider hooks and generic fallback envelopes.\n- Expanded tests and the permanent Google auth proof script for API-key and OAuth staging behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\nValidated locally at PR head `a1bfe44605`.\n\n```text\npnpm test src/agents/auth-profiles/google.test.ts src/agents/cli-runner/prepare.test.ts extensions/google/setup-api.test.ts extensions/google/index-harness-registration.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/provider-catalog-shared.test.ts\n```\n\nResult: 3 Vitest shards passed, 83 tests passed.\n\n```text\npnpm tsx scripts/proof-google-auth-replacement.ts\n```\n\nResult: passed. The proof verifies Google API-key selection, Gemini CLI OAuth selection, isolated Gemini CLI auth home staging, inherited env clearing, API-key staging through `GEMINI_API_KEY`, absence of OAuth/cache files during API-key staging, redacted proof output, hashed profile-home path usage, and exact selected credential kinds.\n\n```text\npnpm plugin-sdk:api:check\n```\n\nResult: `OK docs/.generated/plugin-sdk-api-baseline.sha256`.\n\n```text\ngit diff --check\npnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/google/cli-backend-auth.runtime.ts extensions/google/cli-backend.ts extensions/google/setup-api.test.ts scripts/proof-google-auth-replacement.ts src/agents/cli-runner/prepare.test.ts src/agents/cli-runner/prepare.ts src/plugin-sdk/core.ts src/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry.ts src/plugin-sdk/provider-model-shared.ts src/plugins/provider-hook-runtime.ts src/plugins/provider-runtime.runtime.ts src/plugins/provider-runtime.ts src/plugins/types.ts\npnpm format:docs:check\n```\n\nResult: all passed.\n\n## What Was Not Tested\n\nI did not perform a live Gemini CLI OAuth login against a real Google account. The deterministic proof exercises the resolver, forwarding, env clearing, isolated auth-home staging, API-key staging, SDK baseline, docs formatting, and focused regression coverage in-process.\n\nI did not run the full repository test suite; the focused suite covers the changed auth boundary, Gemini staging, CLI preparation, SDK export, and registration behavior.\n\n## Tests\n\nAI-assisted: yes.",
